# Negative parallelization core budgets are rejected

A worker count below zero is outside the supported nonnegative budget range and fails before execution.

>>> source
@config { parallelization: { cores: -1 } }

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid value for configuration `parallelization.cores`: parallelization.cores must be a nonnegative integer worker count or null at Span { start: 36, end: 38 }

<<< exit
1
